{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.UpstreamMathlibAdditions","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.UpstreamMathlibAdditions","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Log","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.PSeries","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_pi_half_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_pi_half_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L322-L333","doc":"**Boundary unconditional check:** at `θ = π/2`, the double-angle\nidentity becomes `Cl_2(π) = 2·Cl_2(π/2) - 2·Cl_2(π/2) = 0`, a\ntautology that follows from `Cl_2_pi` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_pi_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_pi_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L309-L320","doc":"**Boundary unconditional check:** at `θ = π`, the double-angle\nidentity reduces to `Cl_2(2π) = 2·Cl_2(π) - 2·Cl_2(0) = 0`.\nUses `Cl_2_periodic` for the LHS and `Cl_2_pi` + `Cl_2_zero`\nfor the RHS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_zero_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle_at_zero_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L300-L307","doc":"**Boundary unconditional check:** at `θ = 0`, the double-angle\nidentity reduces to `Cl_2(0) = 0` on both sides (using\n`Cl_2(0) = 0` and `Cl_2(π) = 0` from `Cl_2_pi`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_double_angle","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L290-L298","doc":"**Conditional theorem (sorry-free).** With the double-angle\nclass in scope, the identity holds. Boundary case: at `θ = 0`,\nboth sides reduce to `Cl_2(0) = 0` directly without invoking\nthe class hypothesis (since `Cl_2(2·0) = Cl_2(0) = 0` and\n`2·Cl_2(0) - 2·Cl_2(π) = 0 - 0 = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle.double_angle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle.double_angle","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L286-L286","doc":"The Spence-Lewin double-angle identity for Cl_2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle.mk","kind":"ctor","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L284-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_DoubleAngle","kind":"class","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L258-L288","doc":"The **Cl_2 double-angle functional equation** (Spence-Lewin\nform, restricted to Cl_2):\n\n  Cl_2(2θ) = 2 · Cl_2(θ) - 2 · Cl_2(π - θ).\n\nThis is the imaginary-part projection of the classical\nSpence-Lewin / Landen identity for `Li_2`:\n\n  Li_2(z²) = 2·Li_2(z) + 2·Li_2(-z),\n\nafter the standard substitution `Li_2(-z) = π²/6 - Li_2(1+z)`\nand taking imaginary parts on the unit circle.\n\nDirect `tsum` proof is blocked: `sin(2kθ) = 2 sin(kθ) cos(kθ)`\ndoesn't decompose into a *linear* combination of `sin(kθ)`\nterms (it's a cross-product), so termwise rearrangement of\nthe `tsum` defining `Cl_2(2θ)` does not produce\n`2·Cl_2(θ) - 2·Cl_2(π-θ)`. The proof requires Mathlib's\n`Real.dilog` (or `Complex.dilog`) infrastructure plus the\nSpence-Lewin functional equation for `Re(Li_2)` and\n`Im(Li_2)`.\n\nWe axiomatise the identity as a typeclass hypothesis with\none field; downstream callers that need the double-angle\nformula take `[Cl_2_DoubleAngle]` as `[Instance]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner_unit_circle_eq_Cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner_unit_circle_eq_Cl_2","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L240-L254","doc":"**Conditional theorem: with the classical identity class in\nscope, the Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm on the unit circle equals\n`Cl_2`.** Since `‖e^{iθ}‖ = 1`, the `log‖z‖` correction term in\n`blochWigner` vanishes, so `D(e^{iθ}) = Im(Li_2(e^{iθ})) = Cl_2(θ)`.\nDerived from the class field — not asserted as `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical.unit_circle_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical.unit_circle_identity","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L237-L237","doc":"The classical identity `Im(Li_2(e^{iθ})) = Cl_2(θ)` for every\nangle `θ` (Zagier 1986; the imaginary part of the complex\ndilogarithm on the unit circle is the Clausen function). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical.mk","kind":"ctor","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L233-L233","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoUnitCircleClassical","kind":"class","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L220-L238","doc":"**Conjecture (sketch): on the unit circle, `complexLiTwo(e^{iθ})`\nhas imaginary part `Cl_2(θ)`.**\n\nThis is the classical identity\n`Im(Li_2(e^{iθ})) = Cl_2(θ)` from Zagier 1986. The Lean\nproof requires Mathlib's `Summable` / absolute-convergence\ninfrastructure for the term-by-term imaginary-part extraction.\nWe record the statement as a typeclass hypothesis, parallel\nto the rest of the §3b-cond pattern. Per AGENTS.md §3b-tax the\nclass field carries the **content** of the conjecture — the\nparameter-quantified identity in the shape of the claim — not a\nbare `True` marker. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable.is_summable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable.is_summable","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L215-L215","doc":"The complex dilogarithm series is summable at `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable.mk","kind":"ctor","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L213-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.ComplexLiTwoSummable","kind":"class","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L207-L216","doc":"**Class form for downstream use.** Some downstream blocks\ntake `complexLiTwo`'s summability as a typeclass hypothesis;\nwe provide both the unconditional theorem above and the\nclass form here for backward compatibility with the §3b-cond\npattern. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo_summable_on_unit_disk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo_summable_on_unit_disk","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L172-L205","doc":"**Theorem: `complexLiTwo` is summable on the closed unit disk\n`‖z‖ ≤ 1` (proof attempt).** Compares each term\n`‖z^(k+1) / (k+1)²‖ = ‖z‖^(k+1) / (k+1)²` against the\nsummable real series `1/(k+1)²` from\n`one_div_nat_succ_sq_summable`, using `‖z‖^(k+1) ≤ 1`. The\n`Summable.of_nonneg_of_le` (or `Summable.of_norm_bounded`)\nMathlib lemma closes it.\n\nNOTE: this proof uses Mathlib API from `Complex.norm_div`,\n`Complex.norm_pow`, and `pow_le_one`. Without local Lean\ncompilation we cannot guarantee the exact lemma names match;\nif Mathlib renames any, the proof needs a one-line patch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.one_div_nat_succ_sq_summable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.one_div_nat_succ_sq_summable","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L160-L170","doc":"**Helper: `1/(k+1)²` is summable.** Standard fact, used as\nthe comparison series for `complexLiTwo` summability. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_reflection_2pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_reflection_2pi","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L145-L156","doc":"**`Cl_2` reflection at `2π`.** `Cl_2(2π - θ) = -Cl_2(θ)`.\n\nProof: `sin((k+1)(2π - θ)) = sin((k+1)·2π - (k+1)θ)`\n                          `= sin(-(k+1)θ)`  (by 2π-periodicity)\n                          `= -sin((k+1)θ)`  (by `Real.sin_neg`).\nThe `tsum` of negated summands equals the negation of the\noriginal `tsum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L123-L143","doc":"**`Cl_2` is `2π`-periodic.** `Cl_2(θ + 2π) = Cl_2(θ)`.\n\nProof: `sin((k+1)(θ + 2π)) = sin((k+1)θ + (k+1)·2π) = sin((k+1)θ)`\nby `Real.sin_periodic` applied `k+1` times (the integer multiple\nof `2π` is annihilated by sine periodicity). The two `tsum`s\nare then equal term-by-term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_pi","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L107-L121","doc":"**`Cl_2(π) = 0` (unconditional).** Every summand\n`sin((k+1)·π)/(k+1)²` vanishes by `Real.sin_nat_mul_pi`\napplied to the natural number `k+1`. The `tsum` of identically-\nzero summands is therefore zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L101-L105","doc":"**Cl_2 vanishes at integer multiples of π (sketch).**\n`Cl_2(0) = 0` is unconditional; for general `nπ` the proof\nuses `Real.sin (k · n · π) = 0` when `k · n` is an even integer.\nWe state only the unconditional case here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_zero_via_oddness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_zero_via_oddness","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**Cl_2 vanishes at zero (unconditional, re-stated using oddness).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.Cl_2_neg","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L77-L93","doc":"**`Cl_2` is an odd function.** `Cl_2(-θ) = -Cl_2(θ)`.\n\nProof: `Cl_2` is a `tsum` of `sin((k+1)·θ)/(k+1)²`. Each\nsummand satisfies `sin((k+1)·(-θ)) = -sin((k+1)·θ)` by\n`Real.sin_neg`. The `tsum` of negated summands equals the\nnegation of the original `tsum` by `tsum_neg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L66-L73","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** at `z = 0`, `D(0) = 0` (by `Li_2(0) = 0`\nand `Real.log 0 = 0` in Mathlib's convention). Note: `D` is\ntechnically undefined at `0`; we use Mathlib's `Real.log 0 = 0`\nconvention for the boundary value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.blochWigner","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L55-L64","doc":"The **Bloch-Wigner dilogarithm** `D : ℂ → ℝ`, defined for\n`z ∈ ℂ \\ {0, 1}`:\n\n  D(z) := Im(Li_2(z)) + log|z| · arg(1 - z).\n\nFor `z` on the unit circle (`|z| = 1`), `log|z| = 0` and the\nformula reduces to `D(e^{iθ}) = Im(Li_2(e^{iθ})) = Cl_2(θ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo_zero","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L48-L51","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** `Li_2(0) = 0`. Each term is `0^(k+1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.UpstreamAdditions.complexLiTwo","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.lean#L39-L46","doc":"The **complex dilogarithm** `Li_2(z) := Σ_{k≥1} z^k / k²`,\ndefined as a `tsum` for any complex `z`. The series converges\nabsolutely on the closed unit disk; outside, the `tsum`\nreturns `0` by Mathlib's convention (which is fine for\nthe boundary lemma below). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:upstream-mathlib-additions","label":"prop:upstream-mathlib-additions","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/upstream-mathlib-additions.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}